# Arbitrary Values and Properties

## Overview
Use square brackets for one-off values and CSS features.

## Arbitrary Values

```html
<div class="w-[calc(100%-2rem)] h-[10vh] bg-[#0ea5e9]">
```

## CSS Variables in Arbitrary

```html
<div class="w-[var(--size)] bg-[color-mix(in_oklab,var(--color-brand-500)_80%,white)]">
```

## Properties

Apply any CSS property:

```html
<div class="[mask-image:linear-gradient(to_bottom,black,transparent)] [backdrop-filter:blur(12px)]">
```

## color-mix

Create tints/shades without extra tokens:

```html
<div class="bg-[color-mix(in_oklab,var(--color-brand-500)_20%,transparent)]">
```

## :has() Support

Use relational selectors:

```html
<div class="has-[[data-active]]:bg-brand-100">
```

## Best Practices

- Prefer tokens for repeated values
- Use arbitrary values for prototyping
- Escape special characters correctly
- Avoid overusing arbitrary values for bundle size
- Combine with @utility for reuse
- Test browser support for `color-mix` and `:has()`
